  "narrative": {
    "backstory_summary": "Goliath noblewoman of House Vael-Korr, from the high mountains of the Flanaess. The house claims cloud giant descent, preserved in traditions, runic markings, and oral history — noble in responsibility rather than wealth. Her sorcery is inherited and instinctive rather than studied; she considers herself a knight first. Years ago, outsiders posing as traders and antiquarians gained access to the family hold, seeking cloud-giant records and relics, then attacked: household members killed or vanished, relics stolen, defenses clearly known in advance. She swore an Oath of Vengeance against the guilty specifically — not their race, nationality, associates, or organization. Since then she has followed the enabling network rather than individual killers, which has drawn her toward Stonehaven.",
    "thematic_magic_direction": ["cloud", "wind", "lightning", "levitation", "flight"],
    "character_flaw": "Certainty. Once she believes she has identified the responsible party, she is slow to reconsider.",
    "party_relationship": "Does not expect to command. Respects the party for repeatedly risking themselves for people who cannot reward them.",
    "campaign_hooks": [
      "Scarlet Brotherhood",
      "trafficking route toward the Wild Coast",
      "Kadar al'Habib",
      "unidentified cloaked operative who escaped the party",
      "material recovered from the temple of Laduguer"
    ],
    "deliberately_unresolved": "Whether the Scarlet Brotherhood actually ordered the attack on her home.",
